; MCPd-Disable-Input - revoke remote keyboard / mouse injection.
;
; Usage from a Shell on the target:
;     Execute SYS:System/MCPd/MCPd-Disable-Input
;
; Removes the SYS:System/MCPd/ENABLE-INPUT sentinel. MCPd reads the
; gate only at startup, so a currently-running MCPd keeps whatever
; state it started with -- you MUST restart it for this to take
; effect.
;
; Note this does not undo a --enable-input flag on a running MCPd's
; command line. If MCPd was launched with that flag, remove it from
; wherever the launch happens (S:Network-Startup, or your Shell
; history) as well as running this script.

FailAt 21

If EXISTS SYS:System/MCPd/ENABLE-INPUT
  Delete >NIL: SYS:System/MCPd/ENABLE-INPUT
  Echo "MCPd-Disable-Input: sentinel removed"
Else
  Echo "MCPd-Disable-Input: sentinel was not present (already disabled)"
EndIf

Echo ""
Echo "NOW RESTART MCPd - a running daemon keeps the gate state it"
Echo "started with. After the restart MCPd should print:"
Echo "  'MCPd: input injection disabled (input.* -> -32003).'"
Echo ""
Echo "Also check that MCPd is not being launched with --enable-input:"
Echo "  Search S:Network-Startup \"enable-input\""
Quit 0
